content.text:
We propose LaneYOLO, a fused perception stack that integrates LaneNet for pixel-level lane segmentation and YOLOv5-lite for anchor-based object detection, with three main contributions: 
• A real-time fusion pipeline that achieves end-to-end median inference latency of 12.3 ms on Jetson Xavier NX while processing 720p frames; 
• A homography-based lane curvature estimator and confidence-aware fusion that raises combined detection accuracy to 95.4% and F1-score to 0.947 on a 6,400-frame Bandung dataset; 
• A deployment-ready software/hardware integration using Jetson Xavier NX, Intel RealSense D435, and STM32F407 for closed-loop low-level actuation, with measured power draw of 17.4 W and operational endurance of 3.6 h on a 62.4 Wh battery.
